      "reason": "Repository integration suite uses fixed schema-decoded fixtures to prove atomic review, races, temporal queries, and restart behavior; schema-derived arbitrary round-trips live with the owning domain and use-case models."
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/epistemic/server/test/integration/EdgeAuthority.pg.test.ts",
      "symbol": "schema-codec-tests",
      "kind": "schema-policy-advisory",
      "status": "exception",
      "ruleId": "SFV4-arbitrary-tests",
      "line": 73,
      "owner": "@beep/epistemic-server",
      "reason": "External-Postgres race regression decodes fixed commands to drive two genuinely parallel repository writers; what is under test is database contention (row locks, the open-head index, the exclusion constraint), not schema laws, and arbitrary-driven commands would make the race non-reproducible."
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/epistemic/server/test/integration/EdgeAuthority.pglite.test.ts",
      "symbol": "schema-codec-tests",
      "kind": "schema-policy-advisory",
      "status": "exception",
      "ruleId": "SFV4-arbitrary-tests",
      "line": 60,
      "owner": "@beep/epistemic-server",
      "reason": "Bitemporal behavior regression decodes fixed commands to drive the real repository transaction and assert exact as-of answers at named instants; schema-derived arbitrary round-trips for LogicalEdgeIdentity, the EdgeAuthority commands, and the EdgeVersion entity live with the domain and use-cases model tests."
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/epistemic/server/test/integration/EdgeAuthority.restart.pglite.test.ts",
